meta {
  name: Preview Library Video
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/virtual/videos/{{virtualVideoId}}/stream
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

docs {
  #864, ADR-0049. Returns a short-lived signed playback URL for ANY video of the Bunny Stream library, so staff can
  watch it before assigning it to a lesson. ADMIN and INSTRUCTOR may both call it: no lesson has to use the video
  and it does not matter who owns the lessons that do (since #861 an INSTRUCTOR sees the whole library).
  {{virtualVideoId}} is the guid of a video: run "List Library Videos" first (it stores the first one) or set it.

  The signed URL carries the CDN token: do not paste it in tickets or logs (this API never logs it, and issuing it
  writes no audit row). It is signed like the student stream (GET /api/v1/virtual/lessons/{lessonId}/stream) and
  expires after the same 4 hours (stream.expiresAt, ISO-8601 UTC). stream.type keeps the constant "HLS" for contract
  compatibility; today the URL points to an MP4. Only a video the library finished (status FINISHED) AND that has
  an MP4 copy (hasMp4Fallback) plays.

  Against a local API (demo / e2e profiles, or without APP_CDN_BUNNYNET_APIKEY / SECURITYKEY) the library is the
  in-memory double and starts empty, so this answers 404 until a video exists, and the URL is the local placeholder
  shape. Against a real library use a TEST library, never production (see the ADR-0049 follow-up notes).

  Success contract: 200 with LibraryVideoStreamResponse: { stream: { url, type, expiresAt }, video: { videoId, title } }.
  Error contract:
    400 INVALID_REQUEST           → videoId is not a plain identifier
    401 AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED   → no token
    403 ACCESS_DENIED             → neither ADMIN nor INSTRUCTOR
    404 VIDEO_NOT_FOUND           → the library has no such video
    409 VIDEO_NOT_PLAYABLE        → still processing, no file yet, failed, no MP4 copy or unknown state (see detail)
    503 VIDEO_LIBRARY_UNAVAILABLE → Bunny did not answer (timeout, error or rejected key)
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.stream.url: isString
  res.body.stream.type: eq HLS
  res.body.stream.expiresAt: isString
  res.body.video.videoId: eq {{virtualVideoId}}
}
